From: Florian Fuchs <fuchsfl@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH net] net: slhc: Use unaligned accessors for the TCP checksum

The TCP checksum can land on an odd offset, slhc_compress() and
slhc_uncompress() access it through a plain __sum16 pointer, which is an
unaligned access.

On architectures without hardware unaligned access support, this can
cause alignment exceptions when accessing the checksum.

Use put_unaligned()/get_unaligned(), as slhc_uncompress() already does
for the IP header checksum.

Fixes: 1da177e4c3f4 ("Linux-2.6.12-rc2")
Signed-off-by: Florian Fuchs <fuchsfl@gmail.com>
---
The issue occurred using ssh over serial PPP with VJ header compression
on an SH system, where it paniced, due to another issue of the unaligned
access handler in a delay slot of sh. (separate fix for the platform)

 drivers/net/slip/slhc.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/slip/slhc.c b/drivers/net/slip/slhc.c
index 1a9b27d..a259b6d 100644
--- a/drivers/net/slip/slhc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/slip/slhc.c
@@ -463,7 +463,7 @@ found:
 		*cpp = ocp;
 		*cp++ = changes;
 	}
-	*(__sum16 *)cp = csum;
+	put_unaligned(csum, (__sum16 *)cp);
 	cp += 2;
 /* deltaS is now the size of the change section of the compressed header */
 	memcpy(cp,new_seq,deltaS);	/* Write list of deltas */
@@ -543,7 +543,7 @@ slhc_uncompress(struct slcompress *comp, unsigned char *icp, int isize)
 
 	if (cp + 2 > end)
 		goto bad;
-	thp->check = *(__sum16 *)cp;
+	thp->check = get_unaligned((__sum16 *)cp);
 	cp += 2;
 
 	thp->psh = (changes & TCP_PUSH_BIT) ? 1 : 0;
-- 
2.43.0
